    <h2>What actually happens after pickup</h2>
    <p>After collection, items are sorted by category at the facility. Working devices with resale demand route to inspection and refurbishment. Non-working devices, damaged units, and old consumer electronics route to material recovery — metals (steel, aluminium, copper) and plastics are separated by type for downstream processing. Data-bearing devices route through data destruction before either flow. Batteries route to chemistry-specific recycling.</p>
    <p>None of this involves landfill or dumping. That's the entire point of routing electronics through an authorised recycler rather than general waste.</p>
  </section>

